WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Transcriber: May Alkassir
المدقّق: Mujtaba Abdelwhab

00:00:17.371 --> 00:00:18.371
welcome

00:00:20.163 --> 00:00:21.829
For the first few years of my life

00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:23.663
,maybe I was extremely introvert

00:00:23.746 --> 00:00:26.621
,I always had a hard time
dealing with people

00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:29.913
I always felt there was
.a big barrier between us

00:00:31.496 --> 00:00:34.787
Also I always had troubles
,dealing with life in general

00:00:34.787 --> 00:00:41.662
I always hoped everything would happen
.quickly without effort, even at first try

00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:46.246
,Until, at that time in my life
I got to know Arabic calligraphy art

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:53.246
which was a safe area for me to
escape from

00:00:53.246 --> 00:00:56.287
.any stress or tension in my life

00:00:56.746 --> 00:01:02.746
At first, I started participating in
competitions in school and I won them

00:01:03.912 --> 00:01:07.829
till I won in high school the first place
,at Alexandria level

00:01:07.829 --> 00:01:13.913
then I decided to continue with
calligraphy, but I started to notice

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:19.996
that people look at calligraphy as just
.a hobby Even though it’s an art

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:23.413
And its rules are set almost
.1,000 years ago

00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:30.996
That made me want to tell people that it’s
more than this and has more dimensions

00:01:31.371 --> 00:01:36.413
to do that I had to start break the
,barrier between me and people

00:01:36.413 --> 00:01:40.496
.also I had to get out my comfort zone

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:47.829
To start this step by step I tried to
begin a new journey and get out this zone

00:01:49.413 --> 00:01:55.246
I started getting to know more activities
.and participating in more competitions

00:01:55.246 --> 00:02:01.996
I really started a new journey and one of
the things I found out about calligraphy

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:06.913
is Typography which is simply a domain
,that integrates two arts

00:02:06.954 --> 00:02:11.746
art of calligraphy and art
.of graphic design

00:02:11.746 --> 00:02:17.954
it’s kind of digiliting calligraphy To 
.make it compatible with the current time

00:02:19.621 --> 00:02:25.288
Of course, we’ve all seen
computer typefaces

00:02:25.288 --> 00:02:28.038
.So are logos in Arabic calligraphy

00:02:28.871 --> 00:02:34.538
Among the domains I’ve discovered is
caligraphity, which is also an integrate

00:02:34.538 --> 00:02:38.788
between two arts, the first one
is the calligraphy art

00:02:38.788 --> 00:02:41.329
.and the other one is the graffiti art

00:02:42.538 --> 00:02:46.121
The graffiti art that we all know
is the art of wall painting

00:02:46.121 --> 00:02:53.121
This art is close to us because we often
.see it around us in streets and cities

00:02:55.413 --> 00:02:59.121
One of the projects I saw that had
,a strong message

00:02:59.121 --> 00:03:04.329
belongs to a Tunisian artist named Alseed
.In a neighborhood near the Moqatam

00:03:05.413 --> 00:03:09.829
He tried to deliver his message by
writing it on more than 50 buildings

00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:15.996
and to be able to see the whole message
.must go up to the Abbey in the Mountain

00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:21.913
The great thing is this work won
.the UNESCO Prize in 2017

00:03:22.621 --> 00:03:28.621
One of the domains where calligraphy is
starting to exist strongly is architecture

00:03:30.454 --> 00:03:35.371
Of course we’ve seen many examples where
there’s calligraphy in mosques around us

00:03:35.371 --> 00:03:38.913
.but it starting to break in recently

00:03:39.204 --> 00:03:45.954
And when we saw that in a mosque built
,in a small village in Alsaed

00:03:45.954 --> 00:03:52.746
Almasona village in Suhag and how much
,this line gave value to this small mosque

00:03:52.788 --> 00:03:58.163
when this mosque started to participate in
competitions, it started to become famous

00:03:58.454 --> 00:04:02.538
until it won the Stone award Prize for
.Architecture in 2019

00:04:03.288 --> 00:04:08.954
The first time I got out my comfort zone
is in 2016 when I participated

00:04:08.954 --> 00:04:13.163
in an exhibition in Tunisia this was a new
.experience which changed my life

00:04:13.371 --> 00:04:17.829
To get out of the space where I always
,show my work

00:04:17.996 --> 00:04:23.663
and to try to make people look at
.calligraphy in a different way

00:04:25.538 --> 00:04:30.204
That made me know about lines
,in Tunisia for the first time

00:04:30.746 --> 00:04:35.204
also it taught me that I must break the
,barrier between me and people

00:04:35.204 --> 00:04:40.621
and I actually started to communicate with
.them flexibly and have the ability for it

00:04:42.288 --> 00:04:47.663
Maybe anyone who’s doing a hobby
,is far from their field of study

00:04:47.663 --> 00:04:52.829
,he’s always faced with this question
?could this hobby be his career or not

00:04:52.829 --> 00:04:56.454
this question were always in my mind
because I studied civil engineering

00:04:56.454 --> 00:05:00.538
which is totally far away
.from art and calligraphy

00:05:02.246 --> 00:05:05.788
Of course there were another question

00:05:05.788 --> 00:05:09.746
after I finish will I complete
?in engineering or calligraphy

00:05:10.288 --> 00:05:15.871
I couldn’t be able to answer this question
until 2019 when I won Dewan prize

00:05:15.871 --> 00:05:21.079
for Arabic calligraphy in Germany that’s
when my thinking started to change

00:05:21.079 --> 00:05:24.496
because there’s starting to be a revenue
I can count on to go this way

00:05:25.413 --> 00:05:32.413
maybe we all know how can scribbles
help us to be better in our life

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:38.996
this is what I noticed as I taught
calligraphy over a long period of time

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:45.038
that people generally feels better
.once they grab a pen and scribble

00:05:45.496 --> 00:05:49.621
I noticed this with two of my close
friends, one of them was an engineer

00:05:49.621 --> 00:05:54.496
He was always complaining to me
how much work in engineering

00:05:54.496 --> 00:05:57.371
is putting psychological pressure
and big burden on him

00:05:57.371 --> 00:05:59.704
.and It affects his life negatively

00:06:00.204 --> 00:06:05.079
Of course, I advised him to start with
a hobby like calligraphy

00:06:05.079 --> 00:06:09.329
Because it helped me before
.and I know it can somehow help him

00:06:09.746 --> 00:06:13.871
And indeed, when he gradually
started to deal with calligraphy

00:06:13.871 --> 00:06:16.163
and I asked him about his experience

00:06:16.163 --> 00:06:20.038
He always said to me that he was starting
to feel that the pressure in him

00:06:20.038 --> 00:06:24.329
was moving on to the paper and coming out
.of me, and I was thrilled by this result

00:06:25.121 --> 00:06:32.121
My other friend was at point in his life
suffering from how he will complete

00:06:32.121 --> 00:06:38.121
or find a way into his life and that he
needs to reorder his life and priorities

00:06:39.496 --> 00:06:45.913
It’s been hard for him but by doing
the calligraphy he started to tell me

00:06:45.913 --> 00:06:52.163
how he sees life in general as a phrase
at first he needs to sort the letters

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:59.163
to give him a word and then sort the words
to give him the phrase he wanted

00:06:59.746 --> 00:07:02.538
and to be able to reach his target
.and see it clearly

00:07:03.538 --> 00:07:07.371
calligraphy could have helped a lot of
people to be better in their lives

00:07:07.621 --> 00:07:12.538
as well, it delivered a lot of messages
in the streets around us

00:07:12.579 --> 00:07:18.788
and made a small village in Saeed
,becomes visible on the global map

00:07:19.871 --> 00:07:23.621
.It’s also why I’m here with you today

00:07:23.913 --> 00:07:27.204
There are people who give
their lives to art

00:07:27.204 --> 00:07:33.788
but art gives lives to people
.streets and cities

00:07:33.954 --> 00:07:35.329
.Thank you

